// Which files markdownlint sees. The *rules* live in `.markdownlint.jsonc`, which this file
// deliberately does not duplicate — cli2 reads both, and keeping them apart means the rule
// exclusions stay next to the reasoning that justifies them.
//
// What this check does NOT do: **semantic line breaks**. Markdownlint has no rule for them,
// and MD013 — the closest thing, a hard column limit — is switched off precisely because it
// fights the convention. Semantic line breaks are review-only, and docs/coding-standards.md
// says so rather than implying this command covers them.
{
	// Respects .gitignore, so node_modules, dist/ and the untracked working files stay out
	// without listing them here. Same reasoning as check-links.mjs enumerating through git:
	// a file the check should skip belongs in .gitignore, not in a second exclusion list.
	"gitignore": true,
	"globs": ["**/*.md"]
}
